@segment   affirmation
@title     The Gateway Affirmation — settled form
@levels    F10
@family    affirmation
@fixed

# Said in phrases, the way a person repeats it. The listener says each phrase
# to themselves as it is spoken, so the narration stops after every phrase for
# about as long as it took to say, plus a second. Whole lines used to be one
# breath each, and the owner's account of that: "Others will get a phrase and a
# half. By the time speech pauses the beginning is forgotten." The wording is
# unchanged; only where it breathes moved.

say Say in your mind. Say to yourself.
pause 4
say I am more than my physical body,
pause 3.5
say because I am more than physical matter.
pause 3.5
say I can perceive that which is greater than the physical world.
pause 6
say I deeply desire to expand.
pause 3
say To experience.
pause 2
say To know.
pause 2
say To understand.
pause 2
say To control.
pause 6
say To use such greater energies and energy systems
pause 3.5
say as may be beneficial and constructive to me,
pause 3.5
say and to those near and close to me.
pause 6
say I deeply desire the help and cooperation,
pause 3.5
say the assistance, the understanding,
pause 2.5
say of those individuals whose wisdom, development, and experience
pause 3.5
say are equal or greater than my own.
pause 10
